2:T6d6,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of businesses benefit most from local SEO?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Any business serving customers in a specific geographic area: home services (plumbers, electricians, HVAC, roofing), healthcare (dentists, chiropractors, urgent care), legal (personal injury, family law, criminal defense), restaurants and hospitality, real estate agents, gyms and fitness studios, auto services, financial advisors and many more. If your customers are local, local SEO matters."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to rank in the Google map pack?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Google Business Profile optimizations often produce map pack movement within 4–8 weeks. Sustained map pack rankings require ongoing optimization, review velocity and citation authority — typically showing strong results within 3–6 months of consistent work."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you manage local SEO for multiple locations?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — multi-location local SEO is a core service. We manage GBP profiles, citations and local landing pages across any number of locations, with consistent brand messaging and location-specific content."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is NAP consistency and why does it matter?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"NAP stands for Name, Address and Phone. Inconsistent NAP data across directories — a slightly different address format here, an old phone number there — sends conflicting signals to Google about your business's legitimacy and location. Consistent NAP across all listings strengthens your local ranking signals."}}]}0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Service\",\"name\":\"Local SEO & Google Business Profile Optimization\",\"descripti